  "A literal": "",
  "A literal is a promise the compiler can keep. It bakes French in and stops treating the other languages as reachable — so there is nothing left to load, and your English is not in the output at all. The page does not fall back to English; English was never built.": "",
  "A variable": "",
  "A variable says the language is still undecided, so every one is built and switchable. This is what you want the moment a reader can change language, or it comes from a URL, a cookie or a header.": "",
